        {
          "name": "comment",
          "value": "<p><strong>PURPOSE</strong></p><p>Simulates pushing an approved order to the downstream accounting system (Dynamics 365). Acts as a placeholder integration so the full approval flow can be tested end-to-end before the real connection is in place.</p><p><strong>WHAT THIS WORKFLOW DOES</strong></p><p>1. Build Push Attempt Record</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Creates a single record containing the order_id and a hard-coded push_result (defaults to \"success\").</p><p>2. Log the Push Attempt</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Prints the attempt to the execution log so the result can be traced and audited.</p><p><strong>OUTCOME</strong></p><p>Returns push_result to the calling agent. The agent then routes the order to \"Successfully Processed\" on success, or to \"Exception/Failed\" on failure.</p>",
          "widget": "textarea_rich"
        }
      ],
